# Normalise line endings across the repository.
#
# Without this a Windows checkout writes CRLF into every file, and Terraform
# then compares a CRLF-terminated local heredoc against the LF copy AWS stores.
# Both CloudFront rewrite functions therefore showed as changed on every plan,
# every line removed and re-added identically. It is only noise — but it is
# noise on the one output meant to tell you what is about to change in
# production, and a plan that always shows phantom edits is a plan nobody reads
# carefully.
*               text=auto

# Anything compared byte-for-byte, or executed by a Linux runner, stays LF
# whatever platform it was checked out on.
*.tf            text eol=lf
*.tfvars        text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf

*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.zip           binary
